@format 1
@id media-removal.in-funnel
@title In Funnel
@section Media removal
@area In Funnel
@entry funnel-drain
@summary Show the conditional post-relay removal of successfully delivered Funnel source media from the current Files docket.
@related media-removal.common.docket-removal
@tag media
@tag removal
@tag funnel

@alias messenger = Cadroue.ShellEngine.LMessenger
@alias app = Cadroue.UIShell.PProgram

[funnel-drain] Funnel relay handling <input>
~ This starts with funnel transfer handling.
[Technical explanation]
- Add a source path to the relayed-path set only when a filename rule resolves a target and LMessengerFunnelDeliverSource reports successful delivery @ messenger.LMessengerFunnelDescribe(...)
> drain-gate

[drain-gate] Post-relay source-removal conditions <decision>
~ The program checks post-transfer source-removal conditions.
[Technical explanation]
- Invoke the Funnel drain seam only when Relay Empty is enabled and at least one source was successfully delivered @ messenger.LMessengerFunnelDescribe(...)
? "Relay Empty enabled and relayed set nonempty" > drain-source
? "Relay Empty disabled or no successful relay" > funnel-retained

[drain-source] Remove successfully relayed sources <process>
~ This step handles remove successfully relayed sources.
[Technical explanation]
- Pass only successfully relayed source paths to LMessengerFunnelDrainSource; the startup-configured UI seam removes those paths from the selected tab's Files docket when present @ messenger.LMessengerFunnelDescribe(...)
  @ app.OnStartup(...)
> map:media-removal.common.docket-removal

[funnel-retained] Funnel source media retained <output>
~ This path ends with funnel source media retained.
[Technical explanation]
= No program Files removal is requested when Relay Empty is disabled or every Funnel item failed/skipped delivery.
